  "worked_solution": "The angles ${45}^{∘},$ ${90}^{∘}$ and ${30}^{∘}$ are special angles, and their trigonometric ratios have the values\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘}=1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+1+\\frac{1}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}+2+1}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}+3}{2}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
